---
const steps = [
  {
    title: "Conversamos",
    description:
      "Me contás tu idea y tus objetivos. Analizo lo que necesitás y te propongo una solución con un presupuesto claro.",
  },
  {
    title: "Diseñamos",
    description:
      "Definimos juntos cómo se va a ver y cómo va a funcionar, antes de escribir una sola línea de código.",
  },
  {
    title: "Construimos",
    description:
      "Desarrollo tu proyecto con código limpio y seguro, y te muestro los avances para que lo veas crecer.",
  },
  {
    title: "Entregamos y acompañamos",
    description:
      "Lo publico, te enseño a usarlo y sigo a tu lado con soporte y mejoras.",
  },
];
---

<section id="proceso" class="section" aria-labelledby="proceso-title">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow reveal">// cómo trabajo</p>
    <h2 id="proceso-title" class="section-title reveal">
      Sabés en qué está tu proyecto, siempre.
    </h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      {steps.map(({ title, description }, index) => (
        <li class="step reveal">
          {/* The <ol> already announces the order; the visible number is decorative. */}
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">
            {String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
          </span>
          <h3>{title}</h3>
          <p>{description}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 14rem), 1fr));
    gap: 2rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .step {
    position: relative;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 10%);
  }

  /* The brand line over each step. Without scroll-driven animations (or with reduced motion) it is simply drawn. */
  .step::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: -1px 0 auto;
    height: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-cyan), var(--color-violet));
    transform-origin: left;
  }

  /* It fills as the step crosses the screen, like the "next project" bar. Longhands: see .reveal in global.css. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
      .step {
        view-timeline-name: --step;
      }

      .step::before {
        animation-name: step-line;
        animation-timing-function: linear;
        animation-fill-mode: both;
        animation-timeline: --step;
        animation-range: cover 10% cover 35%;
      }

      /* In a row they share one position on screen: staggered ranges make the four lines fill one after another, 01 → 04. */
      @media (min-width: 48rem) {
        .step:nth-child(1)::before {
          animation-range: cover 15% cover 25%;
        }

        .step:nth-child(2)::before {
          animation-range: cover 25% cover 35%;
        }

        .step:nth-child(3)::before {
          animation-range: cover 35% cover 45%;
        }

        .step:nth-child(4)::before {
          animation-range: cover 45% cover 55%;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  @keyframes step-line {
    from {
      transform: scaleX(0);
    }
  }

  .step-number {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-cyan);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
